        <mxCell id="c88" value="&lt;i&gt;Outlined: SourceDocumentID. The six rows are three pairs of $7,971.10, a debit &quot;Clear accrued payroll&quot; and a credit &quot;Disburse payroll cash&quot;, posted on &lt;span style=&quot;white-space:nowrap&quot;&gt;2024-01-19&lt;/span&gt;, &lt;span style=&quot;white-space:nowrap&quot;&gt;2025-01-03&lt;/span&gt; and &lt;span style=&quot;white-space:nowrap&quot;&gt;2026-01-02&lt;/span&gt;. They name payroll payments 1, 2646 and 5420, which are not in PayrollPayment. This is an integrity failure: the database declares no foreign keys, so nothing stopped these rows from naming a payment that is not there.&lt;/i&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=12;fontColor=#5D6D7E;fontStyle=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;spacing=2;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="0" y="640" width="860" height="57" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
